.\" man page create by R# package system.
.TH GPS 1 2000-1月 "gps_config" "gps_config"
.SH NAME
gps_config \- Create a GPS model hyper-parameter configuration object.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIgps_config(\fBmaxGenes\fR as integer = 2000, 
\fBcpmNormalize\fR as boolean = TRUE, 
\fBlogTransform\fR as boolean = TRUE, 
\fBzScore\fR as boolean = TRUE, 
\fBpeDim\fR as integer = 16, 
\fBspdMaxDist\fR as integer = 5, 
\fBcoexpressionTopK\fR as integer = 0, 
\fBminCoexpression\fR as double = 0.7, 
\fBdModel\fR as integer = 128, 
\fBnLayers\fR as integer = 3, 
\fBnHeads\fR as integer = 8, 
\fBffnDim\fR as integer = 256, 
\fBdropout\fR as double = 0.1, 
\fBgeneEmbedDim\fR as integer = 32, 
\fBuseSpdBias\fR as boolean = TRUE, 
\fBuseGlobalAttention\fR as boolean = TRUE, 
\fBuseLocalMpnn\fR as boolean = TRUE, 
\fBwindow\fR as integer = 5, 
\fBgruHidden\fR as integer = 128, 
\fBuseUncertainty\fR as boolean = FALSE, 
\fBpretrainEpochs\fR as integer = 30, 
\fBfinetuneEpochs\fR as integer = 100, 
\fBlearningRate\fR as double = 0.0001, 
\fBautofocusGamma\fR as double = 1, 
\fBlambdaDir\fR as double = 0.5, 
\fBlambdaL1\fR as double = 0.0001, 
\fBlambdaPrior\fR as double = 0, 
\fBgradientClip\fR as double = 1, 
\fBearlyStopPatience\fR as integer = 15, 
\fBmaskRatio\fR as double = 0.15, 
\fBtrainRatio\fR as double = 0.7, 
\fBvalidationRatio\fR as double = 0.15, 
\fBseed\fR as integer = 2024, 
\fBsignificanceZScore\fR as double = 0.5, 
\fBcascadeSteps\fR as integer = 5, 
\fBCheckpointIntervalEpochs\fR as integer = 1, 
\fBdenseAttentionMaxNodes\fR as integer = 1024, 
\fBattentionNeighbors\fR as integer = 32, 
\fBattentionRandomLinks\fR as integer = 8, 
\fBattentionHubGenes\fR as integer = 8, 
\fBknockdownResidual\fR as double = 0.2, 
\fBedgeNormalization\fR as string = "sqrt", 
\fBperturbationChannel\fR as boolean = TRUE, 
\fBperturbationChannelGain\fR as double = 1, 
\fBperturbationChannelCoRegulation\fR as boolean = FALSE, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Create a GPS model hyper-parameter configuration object.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBmaxGenes\fB \fR\- 
 maximum number of genes used for modelling; \fB0\fR disables the high variance filter and
 keeps every gene of the input matrix. When the limit is exceeded the most variable genes
 are kept, together with all transcription factors of the prior network. Default 2000,
 because the global attention layer scales as O(N^2).
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBcpmNormalize\fB \fR\- 
 apply a CPM library size normalization to every sample column before modelling.
 Default \fBTrue\fR.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBlogTransform\fB \fR\- 
 apply the \fBlog2(x + 1)\fR variance stabilizing transformation after the CPM normalization.
 Default \fBTrue\fR.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBzScore\fB \fR\- 
 standardize every gene across the samples (per gene z-score) so that genes with very
 different expression levels share a comparable scale. Default \fBTrue\fR.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBpeDim\fB \fR\- 
 dimension of the Laplacian positional encoding, that is, the number of the smallest
 non-trivial Laplacian eigenvectors that are projected into the node embedding. \fB0\fR
 disables the positional encoding. Default 16.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBspdMaxDist\fB \fR\- 
 maximum shortest path distance that receives its own attention bias bucket; longer and
 disconnected gene pairs are merged into dedicated buckets. The bucket count is
 \fBspdMaxDist + 2\fR. Default 5.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBcoexpressionTopK\fB \fR\- 
 number of co-expression edges that are added for every gene (the GEARS style covariance
 graph); \fB0\fR keeps the prior regulatory edges only. Default 0.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBminCoexpression\fB \fR\- 
 minimum absolute Pearson correlation required for a co-expression edge. Only used when
 \fBcoexpressionTopK\fR is greater than zero. Default 0.7.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBdModel\fB \fR\- 
 hidden dimension of the model (\fBd_model\fR). Must be divisible by \fBnHeads\fR. Default 128.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBnLayers\fB \fR\- 
 number of stacked GPS fusion layers, that is, the number of message passing hops that can
 be captured. Default 3.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBnHeads\fB \fR\- 
 number of attention heads of the global attention branch. Must divide \fBdModel\fR.
 Default 8.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBffnDim\fB \fR\- 
 hidden dimension of the feed forward network inside every GPS layer. Default 256.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBdropout\fB \fR\- 
 dropout rate applied to the GRU output representation; must be in \fB[0, 1)\fR.
 Default 0.1.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBgeneEmbedDim\fB \fR\- 
 dimension of the learnable gene identity embedding. Default 32.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBuseSpdBias\fB \fR\- 
 enable the Graphormer style shortest path attention bias. Switching it off is the
 ablation setting for "global attention without topology awareness". Default \fBTrue\fR.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBuseGlobalAttention\fB \fR\- 
 enable the global attention branch; \fBFalse\fR degenerates the model into a pure GNN.
 Default \fBTrue\fR.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBuseLocalMpnn\fB \fR\- 
 enable the local message passing branch; \fBFalse\fR degenerates the model into a pure
 Transformer. Default \fBTrue\fR.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBwindow\fB \fR\- 
 length of the input time window (\fBw\fR); at least 2 and at most the number of distinct
 time points minus one. Default 5.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBgruHidden\fB \fR\- 
 hidden dimension of the GRU time encoder. Default 128.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBuseUncertainty\fB \fR\- 
 add a softplus variance head and switch the main loss to the Gaussian negative log
 likelihood, so the model reports a per-gene uncertainty together with the prediction.
 Default \fBFalse\fR.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBpretrainEpochs\fB \fR\- 
 number of epochs of the masked reconstruction pre-training stage; \fB0\fR skips it.
 Default 30.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBfinetuneEpochs\fB \fR\- 
 maximum number of epochs of the next-step prediction fine-tuning stage. Default 100.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBlearningRate\fB \fR\- 
 Adam learning rate used by both training stages. Default 0.0001.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBautofocusGamma\fB \fR\- 
 exponent increment of the autofocus loss, the total exponent is \fB2 + autofocusGamma\fR;
 larger values put more weight on strongly changed genes. Default 1.0.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBlambdaDir\fB \fR\- 
 weight of the direction aware loss term. Default 0.5.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBlambdaL1\fB \fR\- 
 weight of the L1 sparse regularization term. Default 0.0001.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBlambdaPrior\fB \fR\- 
 weight of the prior distance regularization term; it is only meaningful for a learnable
 adjacency matrix and therefore defaults to 0 in the current fixed \fBA_prior\fR version.
 Default 0.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBgradientClip\fB \fR\- 
 global L2 norm clip threshold applied to the gradients before every Adam step;
 \fB0\fR disables the clipping. Default 1.0.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBearlyStopPatience\fB \fR\- 
 number of consecutive epochs without validation improvement before the fine-tuning stage
 stops and rolls back to the best parameters; \fB0\fR disables early stopping. Default 15.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmaskRatio\fB \fR\- 
 fraction of genes whose last time frame is masked during the pre-training stage; must be
 in \fB[0, 1)\fR. Default 0.15.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBtrainRatio\fB \fR\- 
 fraction of the sliding windows used for training; the split is always performed in time
 order, never randomly. Default 0.7.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBvalidationRatio\fB \fR\- 
 fraction of the sliding windows used for validation (early stopping).
 \fBtrainRatio + validationRatio\fR must be smaller than 1. Default 0.15.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBseed\fB \fR\- 
 random seed of the parameter initialization, the dropout masks and the pre-training masks;
 a fixed seed makes the whole run reproducible. Default 2024.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBsignificanceZScore\fB \fR\- 
 a gene is flagged as significantly changed when the absolute Z-score of its perturbation
 effect exceeds this threshold. Default 0.5.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBcascadeSteps\fB \fR\- 
 default number of recursive steps used by the temporal cascade simulation of a virtual
 perturbation. Default 5.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBdenseAttentionMaxNodes\fB \fR\- 
 gene count up to which the exact dense attention (an \fBN×N\fR score matrix) and the exact
 Laplacian positional encoding are used. Above this threshold the model switches to the
 sparse candidate attention (\fBO(N·c·d)\fR) and to the random walk positional encoding, which
 is what makes the whole genome scale (\fBN\fR around 60 thousand) trainable. Default 1024.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBattentionNeighbors\fB \fR\- 
 number of attention candidates per gene in the sparse mode (including the gene itself):
 self + graph neighbourhood (budget truncated BFS) + hub genes + random long range links.
 Default 32.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBattentionRandomLinks\fB \fR\- 
 number of random long range links per gene in the sparse mode; the slots left over by a
 small graph neighbourhood are filled with additional random links, so even a prior network
 without any edge still keeps a global receptive field. Default 8.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBattentionHubGenes\fB \fR\- 
 number of high degree genes included as global hubs in every candidate set of the sparse
 mode. Default 8.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBknockdownResidual\fB \fR\- 
 the fraction of the wild type expression level that is kept for the target gene of an in
 silico knockdown experiment, applied in linear CPM space on the baseline of the
 current cell context: `cpm_mut = knockdownResidual * cpm_ctrl`, then transformed back
 to `log2(CPM + 1)`. `0.2` corresponds to the CRISPRi setting of the Virtual Cell
 Challenge (more than 80 percent on target knockdown). Default 0.2.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBedgeNormalization\fB \fR\- 
 how the graph convolution normalises the aggregated edge weights: \fB"mean"\fR (the legacy
 convex averaging, attenuates a single gene perturbation by about 1e-4 after three hops),
 \fB"sqrt"\fR (default, keeps about 5 to 8 times more magnitude per hop) or \fB"sum"\fR (no
 normalisation, strongest but easiest to saturate).
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBperturbationChannel\fB \fR\- 
 inject the change of the perturbed gene into the input window of its downstream targets
 along the prior edges, so a knockdown does not have to survive several rounds of degree
 normalisation. Default TRUE.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBperturbationChannelGain\fB \fR\- 
 injection gain of the perturbation channel; \fB0\fR disables it. Default 1.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBperturbationChannelCoRegulation\fB \fR\- 
 when the perturbed gene has no outgoing edge (every non transcription factor in a
 TF to target prior), spread its change to the genes sharing the same upstream regulators.
 Heuristic, therefore FALSE by default.
. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a validated [GPSConfig](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.GPS.Config.GPSConfig) object
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
The returned [GPSConfig](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.GPS.Config.GPSConfig) object (registered as the \fBgps_config\fR R# type)
 is accepted by the \fBconfig\fR argument of the \fBgps::build_gps\fR api and controls the
 whole pipeline: data preprocessing, graph encoding, the GPS fusion backbone, the GRU
 time encoder, the training schedule and the default behaviour of the virtual
 perturbation analysis.
 


 


 Every argument is optional and carries exactly the same default value as the
 corresponding property of [GPSConfig](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.GPS.Config.GPSConfig), so calling \fBgps_config()\fR without
 any argument is equivalent to \fBnew("gps_config")\fR. The assembled object is validated
 by [GPSConfig.Validate()](cref:M:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.GPS.Config.GPSConfig.Validate) before it is returned: an invalid combination (for
 example \fBnHeads\fR not dividing \fBdModel\fR, \fBwindow\fR smaller than 2, or
 \fBtrainRatio + validationRatio\fR greater than or equal to 1) raises an
 [ArgumentException](cref:T:System.ArgumentException) instead of failing later during training.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
GPS
